.TH ZAP 1 "October 2026" "zap 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zap \- native Zig AUR helper using libalpm and systemd run0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zap
.I command
.RI [ packages ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
zap searches repository and AUR packages, resolves dependencies, reviews
PKGBUILDs, builds packages as the invoking user, and runs native libalpm
transactions through systemd run0 and polkit. It never builds as root.
System changes require an installed root-owned /usr/bin/zap and a terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search TERM (-Ss)
Search cached repositories and live AUR metadata.
.TP
.B info PACKAGES (-Si)
Display package details, dependencies and update dates.
.TP
.B install PACKAGES (-S)
Review, build and install packages and their dependencies.
.TP
.B build PACKAGES
Review and build AUR packages without installing. Build dependencies must
already be installed.
.TP
.B get PACKAGES
Fetch AUR sources into the user cache without executing them.
.TP
.B upgrade (-Syu)
Refresh and upgrade repositories, then upgrade installed AUR packages.
.TP
.B updates (-Qu)
Check cached repositories and live AUR for newer versions.
.TP
.B list [PACKAGES] (-Q)
List installed versions, installation dates and reasons.
.TP
.B foreign (-Qm)
List installed packages absent from repositories.
.TP
.B remove PACKAGES (-R)
Remove packages with native dependency checks.
.TP
.B orphans
List dependency packages without required or optional users.
.TP
.B autoremove
Review and remove orphan dependencies.
.TP
.B clean
Confirm and clear the user's AUR source/build cache.
.TP
.B version (--version)
Display the version and libalpm ABI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Skip builds, escalation and system changes. Install/build plans can fetch
sources and ask for a provider. Final repository changes are resolved by
libalpm during the actual transaction. get always fetches sources.
.TP
.B --devel
Include installed -git, -svn, -hg and -bzr packages for rebuild during updates
or upgrade.
.TP
.B --recursive
Also remove unneeded dependencies with remove.
.TP
.B --nosave
Discard backup configuration during remove. -Rns combines --recursive and
--nosave.
.SH DATES
All dates are UTC. AUR results show last modification. Repository results
show build dates. Local listings show installation dates.
.SH SECURITY
PKGBUILDs execute arbitrary code as your user after review. Review does not
sandbox that code. Every system transaction requires a separate final
confirmation and uses configured signature policies, ALPM locks and hooks.
Approved archives are copied into private root-owned staging and checked
against their SHA-256 digests before installation. AUR upgrades span several
transactions; earlier successful installs remain if a later build fails.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/pacman.conf
Repository configuration and package/signature policies.
.TP
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/zap, $HOME/.cache/zap
User-owned AUR source and build cache.
.TP
.B /usr/bin/zap
Root-owned executable used by the transaction worker.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal styling.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Absolute user cache directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 130 on a cancelled operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR run0 (1),
.BR libalpm (3)
